<title>SPAIN: Spain's Jan trade deficit narrows to 109.1 bln pta.</title>
<headline>Spain's Jan trade deficit narrows to 109.1 bln pta.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's custom-cleared trade deficit narrowed to 109.1 billion pesetas in January down from a 161.5 billion peseta deficit in December 1996.</p>
<p>The customs department of the economy ministry gave the following figures (billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE		JAN 97	DEC 96	 JAN 96</p>
<p> Exports			1,079.4    1,167.9	 959.8</p>
<p> Imports			1,188.5    1,329.4     1,133.1</p>
<p> Deficit			 -109.1     -161.5	-173.3</p>
<p> Deficit yr to date	  -109.1   -2,504.7	-173.3</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are customs-cleared data.</p>
<p> TRADE BALANCE WITH EU  JAN 97	  DEC 96	JAN 96</p>
<p> Exports		    777.2	   804.4	  731.2</p>
<p> Imports		    737.8	   909.7	  721.4</p>
<p> Surplus/deficit	   39.3	  -105.3	    9.8</p>
<p> Sur/def yr to date	39.3	  -988.7	    9.8</p>
</text>
